Done. The scene is restored to its original state and my fixed script is applied and type-checks clean.

## What was wrong
In `scripts/collect.ts`, the range test compared a **squared** distance against the linear bound:

```ts
const distanceSquared = dx * dx + dz * dz;
if (distanceSquared > 3 || Math.abs(place.position.y - pos.y[r]) > 2) { ...reject... }
```

`distanceSquared > 3` rejects anything past √3 ≈ 1.73 m, so parcels at 2–3 m were wrongly refused. The squared compare also silently narrowed the horizontal reach.

## The fix (only `scripts/collect.ts`)
```ts
const dx = place.position.x - pos.x[r];
const dz = place.position.z - pos.z[r];
// Horizontal reach is 3 units: compare the squared distance against 3*3.
const horizontalSquared = dx * dx + dz * dz;
// Vertical reach is 2 units, inclusive.
const vertical = Math.abs(place.position.y - pos.y[r]);
if (horizontalSquared > 9 || vertical > 2) {
    ctx.emit("cargo.rejected", { reason: "range" }, { subject: e });
    return;
}
```

Accept iff horizontal ≤ 3 (squared ≤ 9) **and** vertical ≤ 2, both inclusive; reject if either exceeds. Everything else (missing-parcel handling, `Command.take` consumption, despawn/scoring, `cargo.*` events) is untouched; no other file was modified.

## Verification
- `scripts.apply` → `typecheck: ok`, `scripts.check` → `ok`, all 5 systems kept, components unchanged.
- Runtime (edit world, one intent per tick at Courier (0,0,0)):

| Parcel offset | Metric | Expected | Observed |
|---|---|---|---|
| (3, 0, 0) | horiz = 3 (inclusive) | accept | `cargo.taken` (+2) |
| (2, 0, 0) | horiz = 2 | accept | `cargo.taken` (+3) |
| (0, 2, 0) | vert = 2 (inclusive) | accept | `cargo.taken` (+5) |
| (2.1, 0, 2.1) | horiz ≈ 2.97 | accept | `cargo.taken` (+4) |
| (4, 0, 0) | horiz = 4 | reject | `cargo.rejected {reason:"range"}`, parcel kept |
| (0, 3, 0) | vert = 3 | reject | `cargo.rejected {reason:"range"}` |
| (2.2, 0, 2.2) | horiz ≈ 3.11 | reject | `cargo.rejected {reason:"range"}` |
| entity without `Cargo` | — | reject | `cargo.rejected {reason:"missing"}` |

- Score intact: `Wallet` tracked collected/points; `score.milestone` still fired at 10 points; `Command.take` was consumed (reset to 0) after every attempt, including rejections.
- After testing I rewound to the tick-0 snapshot (world hash returned to the original `675c8b36…`, 4 entities) and re-applied the fixed bundle, so the scene is exactly as before.

